# XCU ngettext
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# no message catalogs are installed: TEXTDOMAINDIR points at an empty
# directory and LC_ALL is C, so the only observable result is the
# untranslated text (the msgid, or for ngettext the default singular or
# plural); translations are untestable portably because the locale names
# that select a catalog are not specified.

assertion  XCU.ngettext.001
anchor     utilities/ngettext.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/ngettext.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      2024
says       With no catalog the msgid is written for n equal to 1 and the
           msgid_plural otherwise, whether the domain comes from an operand,
           -d or TEXTDOMAIN; n is read as a decimal integer so 001 means 1.
test       t/001-plural-selection.sh

assertion  XCU.ngettext.002
anchor     utilities/ngettext.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/ngettext.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       -e processes C escape sequences in msgid and msgid_plural; -E
           leaves them alone.
test       t/002-escapes.sh

assertion  XCU.ngettext.003
anchor     utilities/ngettext.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/ngettext.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       n of 0 and a large n select the plural.
test       t/003-large-n.sh
